# "Put a guest named Maria at table 1.": the place-verb form of the named add with a place. The catalog frame acts.make.name.place takes only the verb "make" (add, make, create ...)
# so the frame acts.make.name.p (place verb, value = rest) read "Maria at table 1" as the name. Same shape, place verbs, one priority higher than acts.make.name.p.
@pat.plan.seating.make.name.place.p core.pattern
    match="[$lang.lead.filler|pls|plz]? [$lang.lead.filler|pls|plz]? [$lang.lead.polite]? [$acts.verb.place] [$acts.det]? {thing:words} [called|named] {value:words} {rel:lex.acts.rel} [$acts.det]? {place:rest} [$lang.tail.filler|from_now_on|from_now|from_today|from_here_on|please]?"
    emit="@{_} core.request action=plan.seating.make arg.thing=\"{thing}\" arg.value=\"{value}\" arg.rel=\"{rel}\" arg.place=\"{place}\" arg.text=\"{segment}\""
    kind=request
    priority=15
    tabPriority=23
    tabOnly=true
    example="Put a guest named Ann at table 1."
    canonical="Put a guest named Ann at table 1."
